Different bird species are attracted to different types of food. Black oil sunflower seeds are a favorite of many birds due to their high oil content and relatively thin shells. White-striped sunflower seeds are larger with thicker shells, which can deter smaller birds. Thistle seeds, also known as nyjer seeds, are particularly attractive to finches. Suet, a high-energy food made from animal fat, is great for insect-eating birds and woodpeckers, especially during colder months. Peanuts, both shelled and unshelled, are enjoyed by jays, woodpeckers, and other larger birds. Offering a variety of these foods will increase the diversity of birds visiting your yard.

