Cats need a balanced diet of protein, fats, and a small amount of carbohydrates, but some foods are better than others. Cooked chicken or turkey without skin or bones is a great source of lean protein. Many cats also enjoy cooked fish like salmon, which is rich in omega-3 fatty acids for a healthy coat. Small amounts of certain vegetables like steamed broccoli or green beans can add fiber to their diet. Remember to avoid foods like chocolate, onions, garlic, grapes, and raisins, which are toxic to cats. Always consult with your vet for the best dietary advice for your furry friend.

